  "query_preview": "..\nSynoptic Setup: \n\nZonal flow in place over the region will remain in place through\nFriday. An upper disturbance will move in Friday night as a\nsurface low moves east through the area. Rising heights ahead of\nthis low will allow for warming temperatures Friday and Saturday.\nClouds departing early Friday should allow the sun Friday \nafternoon to warm things up. Temps should be about 5 to 15 degrees\nwarmer than today with highs from the mid 60s northeast to the\nupper 70s southwest. With a warm front moving east through the\narea, winds will switch from the SE to the West and decrease.\n\nOn Saturday, the upper flow turns NW with a weak (1023mb) surface\nhigh dropping SE across the area. This will allow for sunshine and\na lighter wind, but slightly cooler than Friday.\n\nThe surface high then moves to our east with a surface low\ndeveloping over southern Alberta Sunday night. The pressure\ngradient will allow for increased S and SE winds with them peaking\nSunday night.\n\nAnother warm front moves east through the area Monday and winds\nonce again turn West. With abundant sunshine, temps should reach\nthe 70s and 80s. This should be the warmest day of the forecast \nperiod.\n\nAbout Tuesday, a trough or cool front will be moving through. Look\nfor highs to be a little cooler with temps reaching the 70s. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nThe NBM seemed to handle all elements well today, so no changes\nwere made. TFJ",
